{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_10_observability_03_correlation_ids_correlation_ids", "label": "Correlation and request IDs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-10-observability/03-correlation-ids.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Generate or accept one id at the edge and thread it through logs, outbound calls, jobs, and errors until the work is done."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_10_observability_03_correlation_ids_asynclocalstorage", "label": "AsyncLocalStorage for request context", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-10-observability/03-correlation-ids.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Preserves the id across await points without threading an extra argument. Enter the context once at the edge."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_10_observability_03_correlation_ids_x_request_id", "label": "x-request-id", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-10-observability/03-correlation-ids.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Trust a well-formed incoming header from your own edge, mint a UUID when missing, echo it on the response. Validate length and charset."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_10_observability_03_correlation_ids_persist_id_on_jobs", "label": "Persist request id on job payloads", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-10-observability/03-correlation-ids.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Otherwise background failures are orphaned from the HTTP request that caused them. Re-enter ALS in the worker."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_10_observability_03_correlation_ids_als_no_cross_thread", "label": "A